      "title": "WFP Madagascar Country Brief, October 2026",
      "description": "Please refer to the attached file. 770,028 people assisted in September 2026 USD 597,169 cash transferred in September 2026 USD 83.5 million required in the next six months (November 2026 \u2013 April 2027) KEY HIGHLIGHTS Food insecurity is projected to worsen during the 2026/27 lean season, with 3.72 million people expected to face IPC Phase 3 or above in October\u2013February, including nearly 426,000 in Phase 4. WFP requires USD 84.7 million for October 2026\u2013March 2027, as it prepares preventive nutrition distributions and strengthens cyclone-season readiness. WFP assisted 770,028 people through in-kind food assistance and cash-based transfers in September, with cash transfers totaling USD 597,169. In preparation for the lean season, WFP began pre-positioning food with government partners for preventive nutrition distributions scheduled to start in November. WFP began the 2026/27 school year with activities in 1,126 schools. A new Lions Clubs International Foundation- and WFP USA-funded project will pilot direct food purchases between schools and farmers\u2019 organizations, linking school meals to local food supply.",
